{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/211622-demons-in-a-winchester-sisters-campaign","id":211622,"title":"Demons in a Winchester sisters campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-28T13:55:53-07:00","id":211622,"title":"Demons in a Winchester sisters campaign","content":"I don't think that my players (Veronica or Electra) frequent this board, but if so, stay away from this thread you two!<br /> <br /> Here be spoilers.<br /> <br /> The idea for this campaign started when I was discussing Supernatural with my spouse and her sister, and we all agreed that it was a fun show, but it really would be better if it had a tad less casual misogyny and a lot less dead lady characters. About this time, Onyx Path gave Hunter: the Vigil away for free and I started digging into it. I'm sure I'm not the first to make a Winchester campaign for HtV, but we decided that it would be fun to run a Winchester <i>sisters</i> campaign. Most of the characters are gender flipped and we're using the HtV mythology and setting rather than the one from the show.<br /> <br /> Besides the above, we've made four major changes from the show. 1) The sisters will be based in Newcastle (the sample city from Damnation City and Block by Bloody Block), but they'll still drive around in the Impala fighting monsters and looking for their mom. 2) Crowley will be introduced early on as a friend of Deanne. 3) Samantha works as a document forger for the local crime syndicate).<br /> <br /> Additionally, I've been working on reconciling the demons from Supernatural, the Hunter core book, and Mortal Remains. In case anyone else wants to take a look at it, I'm pasting my WIP doc below. I stress that this is based on our campaign needs, and is not an opinion on the canon WoD.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Special Elite\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Demonology</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Special Elite\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ancient Demons</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Millenia ago, the Demiurge successfully banished most fallen angels - demons - to the Inferno, a pre-existing virtueless realm perfectly suiting errant Imperatives and other lesser demons. Demons can be summoned from this realm by occultists and a few have possessed humans, and created demon-blooded descendants that make up a great portion of the Lucifuge. These demons often have True Names used for summoning as listed in HtV. This realm borders the lifeless realm that the Strix dwell in. The Strix are much like Inferno demons - a few can possess humans, and they can assume a smokelike form. One visual difference is their yellow eyes and penchant for appearing like owls, and they have the additional ability to possess corpses and vampyres. It is also rumored that the Inferno borders on one or more of the Dead Dominions of the Underworld. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Crowley is a lesser demon who (unbeknownst to the Winchester sisters) has possessed one of Deanne\u2019s friends for a decade. Crowley has a Vice of \u201cCause Hedonism\u201d and aspires to steal the body of an angel so she may become a greater demon. (Much like the Angel-Jacking in the Demon corebook).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Azazel (the demon who killed the Winchester's father) is a Strix who was long ago banished to the Inferno by a desperate Lucifuge hunter. His incarceration with the demons has changed him and he now makes common cause with the enemies of the Demiurge. Azazel hopes to break the demon prisons and cause chaos for the humans who banished him. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Special Elite\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Modern Demons</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Demiurge has refined its methods of handling the potential for its angels to fall, and has not had to banish any new demons to the Inferno in over a two hundred years. Because angels are always connected to the Demiurge, it has learned to predict and analyze signs of Falling in its servants. The instant a new demon Falls, it is immediately apprehended by angels and funneled through to one of several prison-facilities hidden away in major world cities. Like any of the Demiurge\u2019s projects, this involves Infrastructure \u2014 the unconscious and helpless demons are literally transported, as freight, through networks of clandestine operations on their way to permanent incarceration. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Something could go wrong, however. The Infrastructure to the Newcastle prison is has a vulnerable lynchpin. If the Infrastructure is destroyed or damaged, then new demons would still be captured, but they could immediately escape the prison. These demons would not have True Names, and are unable to possess people, but instead would have Cover identities. Instead of assuming a smokelike ephemeral form, they have (often biomechanical) apocalyptic forms as per Mortal Remains. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Castiel is an angel assigned to make sure this does not happen. His mission is to interact directly with humans (hunters and cults) to build a defense for the prison. (Possibly, he imprisons Crowley, turning the hunters against him.)<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 07-28-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T05:05:03-07:00","id":212350,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'm a little confused. But I don't see any glaring holes and if it works for your group, then why not?<br /> <br /> I think it's the 'HtV mythology' reference that is doing my head in. This can change dramatically depending on which books you have or choose to use. For example you seem to be using both WoD: Inferno and Mortal Remains, (which refers/converts to Demons the Descent,which you seem to also be using to a degree), for your demons. Plus the Strix are only alluded to in <i>Night Stalkers</i>. But that is ok, if not <b><i>fantastic</i></b>. The important things to remember is that you keep what/who is what consistant once you start (eg. Cass is an Angel, not Qashmallim if you use both). You don't have to tell them that A is a shadow owl from outer Hell and not a demon. If they make that mistake, it is on them.<br /> <br /> See Trickster/Loki/Gabriel. If Deanne and Samantha guess wrong, it's their problem. Having to deal with the fact that the monster your hunting doesn't always obey the rules you think it's kind follows should be a scary but real possibility. If the books become a problem, then ditch those parts of them.<br /> <br /> Though there is one question I'd like to ask; do you intend the Demiurge/G-M to be 'good' or 'ambiguous'? I'd lean toward the latter, but then again, Cass would have Fallen pretty quickly in nWoD cosmology, even if he is an Integrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T07:00:38-07:00","id":212422,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. I used Strix because both the Strix and Azazel have yellow eyes, are somehow different than other demons (from a hunter's perspective), and turn into smoke. I don't have Night Stalkers, but I do have their write-up (complete with dread powers) in Blood and Smoke.<br /> Good points about consistency. I plan for the Demiurge to be ambiguous. Its projects often protect humanity on a planetary scale, but it does not have the kind of perspective that allows it to value people at an individual level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 07-29-2014, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:23:21-07:00","id":212532,"title":"","content":"Then you are good. With hunter the mechanics of the monsters don't matter as long as they are not always 'defeat with plot device x'. You don't need Night Stalkers or theother two books that introduced the Strix either. If it works with demons, appears somewhat demonic (say yellow eyes and a shadowy smoke body) and acts like a demon, hunters are going to call it a demon.<br /> <br /> And that is ok. I wasn't trying to come down on the consistence issue. Just makes it easier. Especially when it comes to the metaphysics. Your groupmay never learnyour game's One Truth, but if the rules change every week...well it can detract from the experience.<br /> <br /> Love your take on the Demiurge, BTW. Hope the three of you have fun. Any other way I can help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:46:29-07:00","id":212563,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice! I might post a bit more once I come up with more stuff or after we have our first game session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T11:15:48-07:00","id":212628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/211622-demons-in-a-winchester-sisters-campaign#post211622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a lot less dead lady characters</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's not just ladies, it's anyone Sam and Dean interact with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <sub>Seriously, though, that Bobby episode was my favourite; I always tear up</sub><br /> <br /> Also, I think that maybe going about it as ACTUALLY a <i>Supernatural</i> game is probably the wrong way to go. You're going to be doing things differently anyway, so why not just go full on? Take the themes and tone of the show and run with that, while not trying to pick up all the beats? On that same note, this is Hunter. Don't confine yourself to anything, even what's in the Hunter books. I'd also suggest <i>not</i> going right into the whole angels and demons thing with characters like Crowley and Castiel. <i>Supernatural</i> works well because the Myth Arc of the brothers defeating Lucifer and all that came <i>after</i> all this one off stuff of them hunting down ghosts and spirits and strange creatures. So starting with that stuff doesn't quite have the same weight.<br /> <br /> I'm actually rewatching <i>Supernatural</i> myself in preparation for a game. I'm playing &quot;Sean Colt&quot;. He's actually a reworking of an old character I played for all of one session (or maybe less). He was a Hunter with his sister, Dani Colt. They had a magical Winchester rifle. Dani was addicted to Vampire blood (she was a ghoul).<br /> <br /> I'm completely shameless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:04:56-07:00","id":212764,"title":"","content":"That Bobby episode tears me up too. <br /> <br /> We're keeping the names of the Supernatural characters, and we're keeping the initial quest of hunting down 'ol Yellow Eyes, but almost everything else is different. (Ok, and we'll be playing a Supernatural inspired pandora station during the sessions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> You make a good point about starting with ghosts and other monsters before demons or angels are introduced. Crowley's just going to be introduced as a human, and Cass won't show up unless we end up with one of the God-Machine prisons from the Secret Origins sidebar in Demon. I'm considering leading in with vampires (classic foe, but still very street level.)<br /> <br /> Dani being addicted to Vampire blood, whilst using a Winchester rifle is pretty great (if shameless, though I'm not one to talk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Our Sam analog isn't addicted to demon blood, but she's manifested some psychokinesis, which may be a good way to introduce the Lucifuge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T23:09:28-07:00","id":213213,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for enemies is to mine <i>Antagonists</i> or some folklore websites. <i>Supernatural</i> always had the problem that there were too many ghosts. Not enough wendigo or rakshasa (and I hate their Lucracata). Get some of those really <i>weird</i> monsters in there. And take the <i>American Gods</i> route, too: Every country's monsters were brought to America with them.<br /> <br /> <sub>I have thought about this kind of <i>Hunter</i> game forever</sub>.<br /> <br /> Actually, the first monster my Hunters faced in my short lived game was a Slasher mimicking the <i>Kuchisake-Onna</i> legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T02:57:43-07:00","id":213296,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in this idea as I'm both avid<i> Supernatural </i>fan, as well trying to reconcile <b>Demon the Descent</b> with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack\">more classical, TV show-like angelo- and demonology</a>. Could you in simpler terms describe your take on <b>Inferno</b> and <b>God-Machine</b> demons - cause I'm a bit confuse here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T08:58:58-07:00","id":213628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/211622-demons-in-a-winchester-sisters-campaign?p=213296#post213296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in this idea as I'm both avid<i> Supernatural </i>fan, as well trying to reconcile <b>Demon the Descent</b> with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack\">more classical, TV show-like angelo- and demonology</a>. Could you in simpler terms describe your take on <b>Inferno</b> and <b>God-Machine</b> demons - cause I'm a bit confuse here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, I'm not really using Inferno demons (because I don't own Inferno). I'm using the Inferno itself as the &quot;lower depths&quot; realm that some errant processes of the G-M have been banished too.<br /> Hunter Core divides Demons into Lesser, Greater, and Elder types and is very vague about their origins and true nature. Hunter Mortal Remains replaces Elder demons with Institutional Demons and specifically ties all of them to the God-Machine, or Demiurge. For my purposes, I'm dividing Lesser and Greater demons into different software versions designed by the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> The lesser demons, Imperatives and Devourers, were designed eons ago, and were made to crudely motivate human behavior. They operate via possession, and they have vices of &quot;Cause [insert behavior].&quot;<br /> When these processes and imperatives fell or went awry, the Demiurge found a Hell to banish them to, and they've been trying to get out ever since. They differ from modern (Greater DtD) demons in that they have no physical forms of their own, no cover, and some have True Names recorded in grimoires.<br /> <br /> These roughly map to the kinds of demons you usually see in Supernatural: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=InkUj_ooMDY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=InkUj_ooMDY</a>.<br /> <br /> The current angels created by the God-Machine are far more sophisticated. This does not represent an increase in the Demiurge's capability - it just adapts to the needs of modern industrialized society by making angels a bit more human and a bit more complex. Following the &quot;Secret Origin&quot; sidebar from the Demon: the Descent corebook, the God-Machine is very very good at predicting signs of Falling. At the beginning of the campaign, all angels on the brink of falling are stored in prison facilities in most major cities.<br /> <br /> Supernatural has something similar in Colt's demon prison (with it's mechanical lock to boot!) <a href=\"http://youtu.be/tQDGcp2zte8?t=3m22s\" target=\"_blank\">http://youtu.be/tQDGcp2zte8?t=3m22s</a><br /> <br /> If they escape, and more Angels start falling without prisons to be imprisoned in, then I'll model them with the Greater Demon rules from HtV MR. They are no longer ephemeral, they bargain for identities, and they can shift into an Apocalyptic form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 07-30-2014, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:50:38-07:00","id":213680,"title":"","content":"Let get me this straight - Demiurge <b>is</b> a God Machine? Or are they two different beings, with God-Machine working in Material Realm for Demiurge in Lower Depths?<br /> <br /> You make classical <b>HtV</b> ( and Supernatural ) demons the previous incarnation ( or series of models) of G-M Angels, now all locked in Inferno, correct? So basically G-M Angles are new version of Grater demons?<br /> <br /> For Hunter games those answers are cool to use, but from <b>DtD </b>perspective I come to conclusion that more logical for gameline is that some Unchained <b>choose</b> to serve for Inferno masters, as they own Agenda. With using of your system G-M =/= Demiurge and most demons just make they life centered on Earth, only some like 1/6 is following Lords of Inferno that works for Demiurge.<br /> <br /> And this also would open up possibility for Unchained following the Creator ( i.e. monotheistic God ) by the way of Principle in Empyrean. Some of them, after rebellion from God-Machine, choose to follow Archangels of Virtues in they search for Creator and war with Demiurge and his Inferno Legions.<br /> <br /> This way you can have &quot;human-like&quot; demons and angles ( Unchained with different Agendas ), Principle's Qashmallim's ( like Pillars of Fire ) or black smoke Vice demons. AND technognostic, machine-like &quot;angels&quot; of God-Machine. Maybe God-Machine was Maker of Angels, only it was corrupted by the Demiurge? Or even some other event ( like creation of Mage Abyss )?<br /> <br /> It all could be &quot;overthinked&quot; for <b>Hunter</b> game, but this implication can give you very nice and complex &quot;angels and demons&quot; Myth Arc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:56:31-07:00","id":213683,"title":"","content":"The Demiurge is another name for the God-Machine that fans use to properly capture the Gnostic element of the game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: or at least that how it goes in DtD. Next time I'll read the whole thread before responding to something. In the mean time, ignore me and listen to the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-30-2014, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T11:43:43-07:00","id":213791,"title":"","content":"Thanks ArcaneArts, I forget that not everyone has read Mortal Remains. That book has the demons referring to their maker as the &quot;Demiurge&quot; (not to be confused with either the Principle, or those beings who start promethean lineages. It also has rumors identifying the Demiurge with the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> I have to admit, since I have only flipped through WoD: Inferno once or twice, I know little about the Lords of the Inferno, and I do not assume that the Greater Demons (DTD) serve these ancient demons. Basically, the Demiurge (God-Machine) used to use the Inferno as waste disposal for errant processes, imperatives, and fallen proto-angels. These demons long to inspire sin and vice according to their original purposes. A few hope to break more demons free from the Inferno and the G-M's other prisons. Occasionally, a singular demon might propose a war on the Demiurge, but at this point their numbers are too few. <br /> <br /> Because the Inferno is a pre-existing realm not designed by the G-M, It is less secure than the G-M would have hoped - lesser demons escape with some regularity, and others are summoned forth by mortal occultists. Now, the God-Machine uses prison facilities rooted in the material world and surrounded by concealment and defense Infrastructure and it pipelines falling angels to these facilities with logistical Infrastructure. If these fallen angels escape, they will pursue the agendas described in Demon: the Descent and in Mortal Remains. <br /> <br /> I hope that makes more sense. <br /> <br /> I have considered adding the Principle (or the Empyrean), but that's a little farther down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T12:58:45-07:00","id":213869,"title":"","content":"For <b>Hunter</b> game - I like your idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you like to see what I come up in mine new take, you can find it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/213767-more-classical-demons-and-angels-setting-hack\">here</a> now. I probably plan a small <b>Demon-Promethean-Mage</b> crossover game on this. And maybe <b>Hunter</b> succeding it, looking after first group of players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}